1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,107
Myth or reality: charging an electric car at home is always cheaper than gas.

2
00:00:05,227 --> 00:00:11,788
On national averages, a gas car costs about one thousand two hundred fifty-five dollars a year in fuel.

3
00:00:11,908 --> 00:00:15,458
Charging an electric car at home, about six hundred two.

4
00:00:15,578 --> 00:00:21,774
In Washington State, the electric car saves about one thousand one hundred ninety-eight dollars a year.

5
00:00:21,894 --> 00:00:26,336
But in Massachusetts, where electricity costs about thirty point two cents,

6
00:00:26,456 --> 00:00:28,674
it saves only about two hundred five.

7
00:00:28,794 --> 00:00:35,569
And in the worst case, with charging losses added, the Massachusetts savings drop to about fifteen dollars.

8
00:00:35,689 --> 00:00:36,824
Basically a tie.

9
00:00:36,944 --> 00:00:39,599
Verdict: mostly reality, but not everywhere.

10
00:00:39,719 --> 00:00:41,828
It depends on your electricity price.

11
00:00:41,948 --> 00:00:46,141
So, is charging an electric car at home always cheaper than gas?
